<p class="ecl-u-type-paragraph">An energy balance presents energy products (solid fossil fuels, oil and petroleum products, gas, renewable energies, nuclear heat, electricity, etc.) of a country and their production, transformation, and consumption by different types of economic actors (industry, transport, etc.). It allows users to see the total amount of energy extracted from the environment, traded, transformed, and used by end-users.</p>

<p class="ecl-u-type-paragraph">Energy balances can be graphically represented through flow diagrams (also called Sankey diagrams), which allow users to visualise the interrelation of energy commodities in a more illustrative and intuitive way. These flows can be combined, split and traced through a series of events or processing stages.</p>

